{"text": "Slide 1\nLarkfield Home Services, Inc. -- Board of Directors, Q3 2026\nPrepared by Rosemary Achterberg-Diaz, CEO\nOctober 20, 2026 | Omaha, Nebraska\nCONFIDENTIAL -- board members and counsel only\n\nSlide 2\nFinancial highlights\nRevenue $4.2M, up 14% on last year\nEBITDA $310K; cash at quarter end $1,180,400\nCredit line with Great Plains Agricultural Bank, loan no. GPA-CL-0044812: $600,000 drawn of $1.5 million\nCovenant test passed; next test 12/31/2026\n\nSlide 3\nTop customers\nBrightway has asked for a 12 percent price cut; decision needed today\nCustomer\tQ3 revenue\tRenewal\nSummit Ridge Property Management LLC\t$1,020,000\t3/1/2027\nBrightway Senior Living Group\t$655,500\tat risk\nAll others\t$2,524,500\n\nSlide 4\nPeople\nCFO Clifton Mbatha will step down November 30 for cancer treatment; not yet announced\nInterim CFO: Yusuf Demirci, controller; offer at $185,000 base\nCliff keeps his options under the Rule 10b5-1 plan\n\nSlide 5\nLitigation\nLindqvist v. Larkfield, No. CI 26-4471, Douglas County District Court\nFormer technician Hunter Lindqvist alleges he was fired after reporting a workplace injury\nCounsel (Dunmore & Kessler LLP) recommends settling at up to $90,000; insurer reserve $75K\n\nSlide 6\nSecurity incident\nSeptember 9: laptop stolen from a van, serial 5CG1337KQZ; disk encrypted\nSeptember 11: logins to payroll from 198.51.100.36 using the account nalrashid\nNoor Al-Rashid (IT lead) reset all passwords; 412 employee records may have been viewed\nSOC 2 audit moved to next year\n\nSlide 7\nDecisions requested\nApprove Brightway pricing response\nApprove settlement authority in the Lindqvist matter\nApprove interim CFO appointment and retention bonus of $40,000 for Mr. Demirci", "kind": "PowerPoint presentation", "detail": "7 slides · 255 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Rosemary Achterberg-Diaz", "Clifton Mbatha", "Yusuf Demirci", "Hunter Lindqvist"], "companies": ["Larkfield Home Services", "Great Plains Agricultural Ba